  "notes": "USAGE:\nThe transitive counterpart of {泊|と}まる (to stay overnight). The subject is the person providing the lodging, and the person staying is marked with を: {人|ひと}を{泊|と}める.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{止|と}める means \"to stop\" and {留|と}める means \"to fasten/pin.\" All three are read とめる but use different kanji.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {友人|ゆうじん}を{泊|と}める: to put up a friend\n- {家|いえ}に{泊|と}める: to let stay at one's house\n- {一晩|ひとばん}{泊|と}める: to let stay for one night",
